		XX  XX	X    X	X    X	X
		X XX X	X    X	X    X	 XXXX
		X    X	X    X	X    X	     X
		X    X	X    X	X    X	X    X
		X    X	 XXXX	XXXXX	 XXXX



mod000		25/3/78		KFH		mas 0

	This!
	The final entry of 'S9' onto 'm.out' was suppressed by ChrisM
	(date unknown) so that the user can type it and can tell if
	the load was successful.  The actual modification was altered slightly
	by replacing the procedure call (in mas21.c) with the close instruction
	(by KFH).


mod001		2/2/78		SWB		mas 0 2[1367]

	Suppresses unnecessary code on 'ORG' directive.
	Suppress '00' output on 'RMB' directive.
	Suppress unnecessary output of last line onto 'm.out' by simple test.
	Line length increased to 132 characters.


mod002		2/2/78		KFH		mas 1[1] 2[1]

	Signal processing added to clean up rubbish in /tmp before exitting
	when 'DEL' or 'QUIT' received.  This exit procedure ('mexit') was
	used in a few other places, for a tidy exit.


mod003		22/2/78		KFH		mas 21

	Altered command line '-l' and '-o' options :

		  mas file [morefiles] -ojack -lfred

	writes 'm.out' to 'jack' and 'm.lst' to 'fred' - may be in any order.
	They may also be path names.


mod004		27/2/78		SWB		mas 0 1[23] 2[23]

	Added '\r', '\b' recognition.


mod005		17/3/78		KFH		mas 0 1[127] 2[12367]

	Use system utilities 'fopen' and 'getc' for i-o. This involved re-use
	of a register variable 'n' in 'mas11.c' as a buffer pointer for the
	initial test for the character '#'. If this test is not successful
	the buffer must be reset as though no characters had been read.
	Similarly the variable 'intptr' was introduced in 'mas21.c' for this
	purpose. The procedure 'getch' in 'mas22.c' dissappeared.  It was
	necessary to redefine 'EOF' as -1 (returned by 'getc').


mod006		28/3/78		SWB		mas 0 1[12] 2[12]

	Extended label length to seven characters by making full
	use of the symbol table.  Added 'LMAX' = max. no. of characters
	in a label.  Improved flexibility of program by adding two 'sizeof'
	tests for the size of a 'symbol' element.


mod007		1/4/78		KFH		mas 0 1[1-7] 2[1-7]

	The old 'mas1.h' and 'mas2.h' were combined into 'mas0.h' (as they were
	almost identical).  Stylistic improvements were made to all programs.
	The dummy first file descriptor (which is immediately closed) was
	changed from 6 (pass 1) and 10 (pass 2) to -1.


mod008		12/4/78		SWB		mas 0 1[157] 27

	A define for the new constant "NSYMBOL"  was entered in mas0.h.
	This defines the size of the symbol table.  Symbol table overflow
	checking was added.
	Similarly for forward/back temporary labels: the new constant is
	NFB and symbol table overflow is checked in "deffb".
	Two resulting error routines: "symtblerr" & "fberr".


mod009		14/4/78		KFH		mas 26

	Segmentation bug fixed (although probably never used!).  With the
	seg -C directive, the segmentation character should remain with the
	global symbols - it was being prepended to the locals on printout.


mod010		21/7/78		SWB		mas 13

	The FCC directive was made more tolerant of strange characters.


mod011		24/7/78		SWB		mas [12][137]

	An include-external-file directive under the name of "icl" was
	implemented. Following the pseudo-mnemonic must be given
	the name of an existing "masable" file. File names can be
	pathnames of up to 30 characters.


mod012		31/7/78		SWB		mas [12]2

	The procedure "digit" was replaced by a macro equivalent "DIGIT".


mod013		10/8/78		SWB		mas 26

	Comment lines are now untouched.
